{
  "_about": "Proof harness for Assets/Scripts/MoveSheet.cs. Start the player with  -sheet:<id> -out:<dir>  (id = a row id below) and it performs that one move on a standing opponent with the AI and keyboard off, at a fixed 60 Hz (Time.captureFramerate = tickHz, so 1 frame = 1 sim tick), and writes <dir>/<id>_side.png, <dir>/<id>_34.png (4x3 contact sheets, tile 480x270, row-major, tile 0 top-left) and <dir>/<id>_log.txt. Tiles are evenly spaced in SIM TICKS from preSeconds before the move starts to the end of the move (move table windup+active+recovery, or the dodge row ticks, plus tailTicks). The 3-pixel bar at the top of every tile: its length = tile index / tiles, its colour = the fighter sim state (green = before the move, orange = windup, red = active, blue = recovery, magenta = roll/dodge, grey = loco/guard, cyan = stagger/down). Optional CLI: -sheetdata:<file> (alternative json), -isolate (render only layer 8 on a flat colour: use when a bridge parapet blocks the side camera).",
